        {
          "case": "nonempty-choice",
          "status": "not_applicable",
          "reason": "Example of Explicit regular quadratic Wick star product: Let $f,g\\in\\mathcal D(\\mathbb R^d)$, let $\\ell_f(\\phi)=\\int f(x)\\phi(x)\\,dx$, and let $W$ be any continuous bidistribution. For the regular quadratic functionals $F(\\phi)=\\ell_f(\\phi)^2$ and $G(\\phi)=\\ell_g(\\phi)^2$, the finite contraction formula is $$ F\\star_W G =\\ell_f^2\\ell_g^2+4\\eta W(f,g)\\ell_f\\ell_g+2\\eta^2W(f,g)^2. $$ The formula is exact in the formal parameter $\\eta$. The displayed finite algebraic/test-contraction computation uses supplied objects rather than choosing elements of a family of nonempty sets; no nonempty-family selection is a separate conclusion."
        },
